## 4. States

| State | What the user sees | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| Default | Available balance card at top, withdrawal amount input, "Withdraw full balance" shortcut, bank account details, active/disabled "Request withdrawal" button, and chronological list of past withdrawal requests below. | Screen opened and balance + withdrawal history loaded |
| Empty (no data) | Available balance shows `0 VND` (or below minimum threshold) with "Request withdrawal" disabled and helper banner; withdrawal history section shows "No withdrawal requests yet. Your completed payout requests will appear here." | Supplier has never made a withdrawal and/or has `0 VND` available balance |
| Loading | Skeleton placeholders for the balance card, form fields, and history list; "Request withdrawal" button is disabled. | Screen opened while fetching `available_payout_balance` and `withdrawal_history` |
| Error | **Validation error:** Inline red message under input (e.g., `"Withdrawal amount must be between 100,000 VND and 1,250,000 VND."`).<br>**Incomplete bank info:** Warning banner `"Bank account details are missing. Update your profile to withdraw."` with link to `S-F01-02`.<br>**Network / submission failure:** Banner `"Changes could not be saved. Check your internet connection and try again."` (`ui-conventions` §4); entered values are preserved. | Invalid amount entered, missing bank profile, or API failure during submission |
| Success / confirmation | Confirmation banner `"Withdrawal request WDR-0042 for 1,250,000 VND submitted."`; `available_payout_balance` immediately deducts the requested amount; the new request appears at the top of the withdrawal history list with status badge `Pending`. | User taps "Confirm withdrawal" inside the `Confirm withdrawal` modal and the request is saved (`FR-05-02`) |

## 5. Interactions and navigation

| # | Element | User action | System response | Goes to screen |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Withdraw full balance | tap | Populates the Withdrawal amount field with the full `supplier.available_payout_balance` | stays |
| 2 | Withdrawal amount | input | Formats numeric value with thousand separators and validates against min/max rules in real time | stays |
| 3 | Request withdrawal | tap | Validates form; if valid, opens the **"Confirm withdrawal"** modal displaying amount and destination bank details | stays (modal overlay) |
| 4 | Confirm withdrawal (in modal) | tap | Submits withdrawal request (`FR-05-02`), closes modal, deducts pending amount from available balance, and transitions to Success state | stays (success state) |
| 5 | Cancel (in modal) | tap | Dismisses modal without creating a withdrawal request; form inputs remain intact | stays |
| 6 | Update bank details link (if shown) | tap | Navigates to supplier compliance & payout profile to update bank info | S-F01-02 |
| 7 | Back | tap | Returns to the Loyalty and payout balance screen | S-F05-01 |

## 6. Screen-level rules

| Rule ID | Rule | Source |
|---|---|---|
| SR-001 | A withdrawal request cannot exceed the supplier's current `available_payout_balance` (excluding amounts already locked in `Pending` or `Processing` withdrawals). | FR-05-02 / BR-05 |
| SR-002 | The requested withdrawal amount must meet or exceed the system-configured minimum withdrawal threshold (`config.min_withdrawal_amount`). | FR-05-02 |
| SR-003 | Submitting a withdrawal always requires explicit confirmation via the **"Confirm withdrawal"** modal before creating the transaction record. | `screen-list` Modals table; `ui-conventions` §3 |
| SR-004 | Only payout balances earned from verified/signed transactions (`FR-03-01`, `FR-05-01`) are eligible for withdrawal; unverified draft agreements are excluded. | FR-05-01, FR-05-02 |
| SR-005 | Withdrawal statuses (`Pending`, `Processing`, `Completed`, `Rejected`) must display both an icon and a text label, never color alone. | `ui-conventions` §3 & §5 |

